; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Misty Mountain Ranges
; CATEGORY: Generative Art & Colour
; LEVEL:    Advanced
; TAGS:     midpoint displacement, arrays, recursion, landscape, color
; SUMMARY:  Grows random mountain ridges by midpoint displacement and paints them in misty layers.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Each ridge starts as a straight line. The middle point is pushed
;   up or down by a random amount, then the middles of the two halves
;   are pushed by half as much, and so on, until the line is rough
;   like a real mountain skyline. Five ridges are painted from the
;   back to the front, each darker and nearer, over a sky that fades
;   from peach to pale blue.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run for a new landscape. Change :rough (0.4 to 0.7) to
;   make gentle hills or jagged peaks.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * midpoint displacement, a classic way to make fractal terrain
;   * arrays: ARRAY, ITEM and SETITEM to store 129 heights
;   * recursion over halves of an array
;   * painting with vertical strokes so nearer ridges cover farther
;     ones
;   * blending a color toward the sky color for distance haze
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Make 8 ridges instead of 5.
;   * Add a sun between the sky and the back ridge.
;   * Make the front ridge black for a silhouette at dusk.
; ============================================================

; DISPLACE fills the heights between positions :lo and :hi of the
; array. The middle gets the average of the ends plus a random push
; of up to :push steps; then each half is done with a smaller push.
to displace :lo :hi :push
  if :hi - :lo < 2 [stop]
  localmake "mid (:lo + :hi) / 2
  localmake "avg ((item :lo :ridge) + (item :hi :ridge)) / 2
  setitem :mid :ridge :avg + (random minus :push :push)
  displace :lo :mid int :push * :rough
  displace :mid :hi int :push * :rough
end

; MAKE.RIDGE builds a ridge around height :base and outputs it as an
; array of 129 heights (128 gaps of 6.25 steps cover 800 steps).
to make.ridge :base :push
  make "ridge array 129
  setitem 1 :ridge :base + (random minus :push :push)
  setitem 129 :ridge :base + (random minus :push :push)
  displace 1 129 :push
  output :ridge
end

; FADE mixes a color toward the sky color by :t (0 = no haze).
to fade :color :t
  output (map [?1 + :t * (?2 - ?1)] :color [200 210 230])
end

; PAINT.RIDGE paints the ground below a ridge with vertical strokes,
; one per array entry. A later ridge simply paints over it.
to paint.ridge :ridge :color
  setpencolor :color
  setpensize 7
  for [i 1 129] [
    penup setxy -400 + (:i - 1) * 6.25 -300 pendown
    setheading 0
    forward (item :i :ridge) + 300
  ]
end

; SKY paints horizontal bands from peach at the bottom to pale blue.
to sky
  setpensize 6
  for [y -300 300 5] [
    localmake "t (:y + 300) / 600
    setpencolor (list 250 - 70 * :t 200 + 20 * :t 170 + 80 * :t)
    penup setxy -400 :y setheading 90 pendown
    forward 800
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
make "rough 0.6
sky
; five ridges, from far and high to near and low
for [k 1 5] [
  localmake "near :k / 5
  paint.ridge make.ridge 150 - 70 * :k 190 - 25 * :k ~
              fade [40 45 80] 0.85 - 0.8 * :near
]
